Relevant columns and their usage  

• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips.start_station_id` : start‑station numeric key that we will join to the stations table.  
• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips.end_station_id`   : end‑station key (stored as STRING, so we CAST to INT64).  
• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips.trip_id`          : lets us view individual trips when exploring.  
• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations.station_id`    : primary key for each station, used in joins.  
• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations.council_district` : numeric Austin council‑district for the station; core field we need to aggregate by.  
• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations.status`        : tells whether a station is “active” (only trips whose start & end stations are active are counted).  
• (condition) `start_station_id <> CAST(end_station_id AS INT64)`          : ensures the trip started and ended at different physical stations.  
• (condition) `sd.council_district = ed.council_district`                  : makes sure the trip both started and finished inside the same council district.  

Below are ten progressively richer SELECT‑only statements (each capped with LIMIT 20 except the last) that you can run in BigQuery to explore the data and finally obtain the requested numeric council‑district value.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at the distinct station statuses
SELECT DISTINCT status
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List a few active stations with their districts
SELECT station_id, name, council_district, status
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status = 'active'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect sample trips with start & end station IDs
SELECT trip_id, start_station_id, end_station_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Join a trip’s START station to its council district
SELECT t.trip_id,
       t.start_station_id,
       sd.council_district AS start_district
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS sd
       ON sd.station_id = t.start_station_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Join a trip’s END station to its council district (casting the id)
SELECT t.trip_id,
       t.end_station_id,
       ed.council_district AS end_district
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS ed
       ON ed.station_id = CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Show trips that start and end in the SAME district
SELECT t.trip_id,
       sd.council_district AS district
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS sd
     ON sd.station_id = t.start_station_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS ed
     ON ed.station_id = CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
WHERE sd.council_district = ed.council_district
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Same‑district trips, but NOT the same station
SELECT t.trip_id,
       sd.council_district AS district
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS sd
     ON sd.station_id = t.start_station_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS ed
     ON ed.station_id = CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
WHERE sd.council_district = ed.council_district
  AND t.start_station_id <> CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Add the “active” filter so both stations are currently active
SELECT t.trip_id,
       sd.council_district AS district
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS sd
     ON sd.station_id = t.start_station_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS ed
     ON ed.station_id = CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
WHERE sd.council_district = ed.council_district
  AND t.start_station_id <> CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
  AND sd.status = 'active'
  AND ed.status = 'active'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Aggregate those trips by council district (top few counts)
SELECT sd.council_district AS district,
       COUNT(*)               AS trip_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS sd
     ON sd.station_id = t.start_station_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS ed
     ON ed.station_id = CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
WHERE sd.council_district = ed.council_district
  AND t.start_station_id <> CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
  AND sd.status = 'active'
  AND ed.status = 'active'
GROUP BY district
ORDER BY trip_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL query – returns the numeric council district
--     with the highest number of same‑district, different‑station,
--     “active station” bike trips.
SELECT district
FROM (
  SELECT sd.council_district AS district,
         COUNT(*) AS trip_count
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS sd
       ON sd.station_id = t.start_station_id
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS ed
       ON ed.station_id = CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
  WHERE sd.council_district = ed.council_district
    AND t.start_station_id <> CAST(t.end_station_id AS INT64)
    AND sd.status = 'active'
    AND ed.status = 'active'
  GROUP BY district
  ORDER BY trip_count DESC
  LIMIT 1
);
```

Running the last statement yields the single numeric value for the Austin council district that records the most bike‑share trips beginning and ending inside its boundaries but at different stations, considering only currently active stations.
